/P 87 0 R
/E (Based on the three main indicators, it is clear that the trial campaign produced varying results across stores, and the experiment cannot be reduced to a single conclusion applicable to all locations. Store 88 recorded the strongest performance, achieving a 217.03% increase in sales compared with its control store, accompanied by a 63.40% increase in the number of customers and a 17.90% increase in average transactions per customer. In contrast, Store 77 recorded a 72.77% decline in sales, along with a 17.65% decrease in the number of customers and a 19.13% decrease in average transactions per customer. Store 86 showed more moderate results, with sales increasing by 4.52% and the number of customers increasing by 6.87%, while average transactions per customer decreased by 3.34%.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
